+# hvir
+
+hvir is an Electron workbench for working with local and SSH-hosted projects. It combines a project file tree and editor with Git status and history, a terminal workspace, browser panes, document review, and integrations for Claude and Codex sessions.
+
+## Features
+
+- Open, browse, edit, and organize local or SSH-hosted project workspaces.
+- Work with multiple terminal sessions, split terminal layouts, terminal search, and terminal-rendered web panes.
+- Inspect Git changes, diffs, commit history, branches, fetch/pull state, and the commit graph.
+- Preview Markdown, Mermaid diagrams, syntax-highlighted source, and document-review changes.
+- Track Claude and Codex session context and usage from supported local harness artifacts.
+- Use configurable themes, terminal settings, keybindings, workspace tabs, and diagnostics.
+
+## Requirements
+
+- Node.js 24 or later
+- npm
+- A native build toolchain compatible with `node-gyp`, required for `node-pty` and the local `@hvir/rename-noreplace` module
+
+On Linux, Electron also requires the system libraries declared in [`electron-builder.yml`](electron-builder.yml). Release packages target macOS on Apple Silicon and Debian-based Linux on x64 or ARM64.
+
+## Getting started
+
+```bash
+git clone <repository-url>
+cd hvir
+npm ci
+npm run dev
+```
+
+`npm ci` runs the project's post-install step, which installs Electron and rebuilds the native runtime modules for Electron's ABI. The development application opens through Electron Vite; use the project picker to choose a local folder or configured SSH workspace.
+
+## Development
+
+| Command | Purpose |
+| --- | --- |
+| `npm run dev` | Start the Electron development environment. |
+| `npm run build` | Type-check and build the application into `out/`. |
+| `npm run preview` | Preview a built application. |
+| `npm run lint` | Run ESLint. |
+| `npm run typecheck` | Type-check main/preload and renderer code. |
+| `npm test` | Run the Vitest test suite. |
+| `npm run verify` | Run seam, ADR, architecture, lint, type, and unit-test checks. |
+| `npm run smoke` | Build the smoke target and run the cross-platform Electron smoke scenarios. |
+| `npm run smoke:macos` | Run the macOS-specific smoke scenario set. |
+
+Install the repository's pre-push hook to run type checks and the local-platform smoke suite before pushing:
+
+```bash
+npm run hooks:install
+```
+
+## Packaging
+
+Build distributable packages on their target platform:
+
+```bash
+# macOS Apple Silicon installer
+npm run pack:mac:arm64
+
+# Debian package for x64 Linux
+npm run pack:linux:x64
+
+# Debian package for ARM64 Linux
+npm run pack:linux:arm64
+```
+
+Artifacts are written to `dist/`. Use `npm run build:dir` to create an unpacked application directory instead.
+
+## Project layout
+
+- `src/main/` — Electron main process, project hosts, Git, PTY, diagnostics, and application services.
+- `src/preload/` — typed and restricted renderer-to-main bridge.
+- `src/renderer/` — React workbench UI.
+- `src/shared/` — shared contracts and domain types.
+- `src/workers/` — Electron utility-process workers.
+- `test/` — Vitest unit and integration tests.
+- `scripts/` — release, architecture, smoke, and project-maintenance tooling.
+- `build/` — application icons, entitlements, installer configuration, and native packaging assets.
+
